00:04:25.891 --> 00:04:31.411
Stanford work on dunes, Fizz.org reports, finds that median grain size is a direct readout

00:04:31.411 --> 00:04:33.631
of how fast the winds were that built the dune.

00:04:33.631 --> 00:04:38.931
Calibration used dunes on Earth, then the same rule was pointed at Martian dune fields

00:04:38.931 --> 00:04:40.251
imaged by orbiters.

00:04:40.751 --> 00:04:45.331
Sand becomes a wind speedometer for active dunes and for ancient dune fields across the

00:04:45.331 --> 00:04:45.991
solar system.

00:04:46.571 --> 00:04:51.611
Only faster winds can move larger particles, so stronger winds leave corsair grains in the

00:04:51.611 --> 00:04:52.371
dunes they build.

00:04:53.071 --> 00:04:57.091
Wind speed estimates taken from those grains match independent atmospheric models.

00:04:57.771 --> 00:05:03.151
Past winds can be rebuilt from dunes preserved in stone, with no direct wind measurement required.

00:05:03.151 --> 00:05:08.371
shared. How the link changes under very different atmospheric densities, or when sand is scarce,

00:05:08.611 --> 00:05:09.351
is still unknown.

00:05:10.011 --> 00:05:14.851
Grainsized distributions measured by a future rover or land or on another world would

00:05:14.851 --> 00:05:18.911
test whether the Earth calibration applies everywhere or needs a local adjustment.

00:05:19.611 --> 00:05:24.811
Shifts in solar illumination and in a spacecraft's power draw could determine position in lunar

00:05:24.811 --> 00:05:30.491
orbit without Earth-based tracking. Growing demand on NASA's Deep Space Network, the antennas

00:05:30.491 --> 00:05:35.231
that tracked distance spacecraft, is the pressure this independent lunar navigation is meant

00:05:35.231 --> 00:05:35.751
